  "notes": [
   "Page covers steps 1-2. Step 1: dark bluish gray side-finger hinge plate (b1) with black 4x4 plate (b2) clutched onto it, with the hinge finger sticking out at the left.",
   "Step 2: four red 2-finger hinge plates (b3-b6) are attached under the 4x4 plate (left, right, front, back), so the plate rests on them. I recorded these as joined edges because b2 was placed earlier and the piece-order convention can't express it.",
   "The identification of the gray piece as 44567a and the exact positions of the red hinges are inferred from small illustrations.",
   "Back page is advertising only (combining the crab, scorpion and bird sets). No building steps, so no pieces or joins were added.",
   "The first page image actually contained all of steps 1-8 (the earlier answer wrongly stopped at step 2). This answer adds b7-b32 for steps 3-8, so every piece in the parts list is now used once (32 in total, with b1-b6 from before).",
   "These additions should be merged with the earlier b1-b6 parts and edges, which are unchanged.",
   "The images are small, so many placements are inferred. Steps 3-8 are assumed as follows. Step 3 adds the last two red hinge plates (b7, b8) and the dark bluish gray 2-finger hinge (b9) under the plate. Step 4 adds the light bluish gray 2x2 (b10) and two orange 1x2 plates (b11, b12). Step 5 adds the two levers (b13, b14, the antennae) and one more orange plate (b15). Step 6 adds the red wedge plates (b16, b17) and the red 1x3 (b18). Step 7 adds the black 2x2 on top (b19), the six black 1-finger hinge plates as lower legs (b20-b25), and the two black 2x4 plates as feet (b26, b27). Step 8 builds a sub-assembly (b28-b32) that attaches at the left.",
   "The step 8 sub-assembly is read from its inset as: red 1x2 (b29) on the gray handle plate (b28), then on black 2x3 (b30), with two orange 1x2 plates (b31, b32) on top. Its exact stacking order and attachment point on the model are uncertain.",
   "Hinge edges link each black 44301a to one of the six red 44302a at port hinge.1. Which hinge goes with which leg is a guess. The dark bluish gray hinge b9 and the gray 2540 (b28) have no other joins recorded.",
   "The gray vertical legs in step 8 are not identified separately. They are taken to be the black hinges and plates already counted, since the parts list has no other pieces."
  ]
 },
